{
  "id": "ku1dw02",
  "title": "CHAPTER 5: CULTURE, ART AND HERITAGE OF PUNJAB",
  "order": 5,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "s1d5afr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.1 Languages"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Punjab's cultural landscape features energetic folk dances, primarily Bhangra performed by men and Giddha performed by women.",
        "Three of the five holy seats of authority in Sikhism (Sikh Takhts) are located within Punjab, with Sri Akal Takht Sahib being the highest temporal seat.",
        "Punjabi literature spans rich classical Sufi tradition (Warish Shah, Bulleh Shah) and spiritual Gurbani poetry, evolving into vibrant modern literature.",
        "Traditional crafts like Phulkari embroidery, leather Juttis, and woodcraft are integral to the state's artistic identity."
      ],
      "id": "9n3dtmy"
    },
