    {
      "id": "6e5rpst",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.5.1 Sikh Takhts (Seats of Authority)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hfqi6bu",
      "content": "There are five Takhts (Thrones/Seats of Temporal Authority) in Sikhism:"
    },
    {
      "id": "jwanegq",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Takht</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Location</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Significance</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sri Akal Takht Sahib</p>",
            "<p>Amritsar, Punjab</p>",
            "<p>Highest seat of Sikh temporal authority; established by Guru Hargobind Ji (1606); faces Golden Temple</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Takht Sri Patna Sahib</p>",
            "<p>Patna, Bihar</p>",
            "<p>Birthplace of Guru Gobind Singh Ji (1666)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Takht Sri Hazur Sahib</p>",
            "<p>Nanded, Maharashtra</p>",
            "<p>Where Guru Gobind Singh Ji passed away (1708)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Takht Sri Damdama Sahib</p>",
            "<p>Talwandi Sabo, Bathinda, Punjab</p>",
            "<p>Where Guru Gobind Singh Ji compiled final version of Guru Granth Sahib; called 'Guru ki Kashi'</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Takht Sri Kesgarh Sahib</p>",
            "<p>Anandpur Sahib, Rupnagar, Punjab</p>",
            "<p>Where Khalsa Panth was founded (1699)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "wi5wobx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.5.2 Important Gurdwaras in Punjab"
    },
    {
      "id": "l1sj34h",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Gurdwara</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Location</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Significance</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Harmandir Sahib (Golden Temple)</p>",
            "<p>Amritsar</p>",
            "<p>Holiest shrine of Sikhs; completed by Guru Arjan Dev Ji; gold-plated structure in sarovar (sacred pool)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Anandpur Sahib</p>",
            "<p>Rupnagar district</p>",
            "<p>Founded by Guru Tegh Bahadur Ji; birthplace of Khalsa; site of Hola Mohalla</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Fatehgarh Sahib</p>",
            "<p>Fatehgarh Sahib district</p>",
            "<p>Sahibzadas martyred here under orders of Wazir Khan (1705)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Chamkaur Sahib</p>",
            "<p>Rupnagar district</p>",
            "<p>Battle of Chamkaur (1704); Sahibzada Ajit Singh and Jujhar Singh martyred</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Tarn Taran Sahib</p>",
            "<p>Tarn Taran</p>",
            "<p>Founded by Guru Arjan Dev Ji; large sarovar; traditionally visited by persons with skin diseases</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Muktsar Sahib (Sri Fatehgarh Sahib)</p>",
            "<p>Muktsar, Fazilka-Muktsar</p>",
            "<p>Battle of Khidrana (1705); 40 Muktay martyred; Maghi mela held</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Damdama Sahib</p>",
            "<p>Talwandi Sabo, Bathinda</p>",
            "<p>Guru ka Lahore; Guru Gobind Singh finalized Guru Granth Sahib here</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Kiratpur Sahib</p>",
            "<p>Rupnagar</p>",
            "<p>Founded by Guru Hargobind Ji; ashes of Sikhs immersed in Sutlej here; associated with Guru Har Rai Ji</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Patalpuri</p>",
            "<p>Kiratpur Sahib, Rupnagar</p>",
            "<p>Where Baba Gurditta Ji (son of Guru Hargobind) died in meditation</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
