    },
    {
      "id": "pfu6gaq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.6.1 Classical Punjabi Literature"
    },
    {
      "id": "wqtcncv",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Author</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Period</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Works / Contribution</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Baba Farid (Fariduddin Ganjshakar)</p>",
            "<p>1173–1266</p>",
            "<p>Earliest known Punjabi poet; mystical verses included in Guru Granth Sahib (Farida Sloks)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Guru Nanak Dev Ji</p>",
            "<p>1469–1539</p>",
            "<p>Founded Punjabi literary tradition; Japji Sahib, Asa di Var, Sidh Gost</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Waris Shah</p>",
            "<p>1722–1798</p>",
            "<p>Epic poem 'Heer Ranjha' (Heer); considered greatest Punjabi romantic poem</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bulleh Shah</p>",
            "<p>1680–1757</p>",
            "<p>Sufi poet; Kafi form; verse critical of religious orthodoxy; humanistic</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Shah Husain</p>",
            "<p>1538–1599</p>",
            "<p>Punjabi Sufi poet; Kafis about divine love using metaphor of Heer</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sultan Bahu</p>",
            "<p>1628–1691</p>",
            "<p>Sufi poetry; Faqr philosophy; wrote in Punjabi (Abyat)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Damodar Das (Damodar)</p>",
            "<p>15th century</p>",
            "<p>Author of 'Heer' (first version before Waris Shah)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Peelu</p>",
            "<p>16th century</p>",
            "<p>Composed 'Mirza Sahiban' :tragic love story in Punjabi</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ulhd67j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.6.2 Modern Punjabi Literature"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Out of the 5 Sikh Takhts, 3 are in Punjab (Akal Takht Sahib, Damdama Sahib, Keshgarh Sahib), while Patna Sahib is in Bihar and Hazur Sahib is in Maharashtra.",
        "Phulkari embroidery is a GI-tagged craft from Punjab, frequently featured in state and national art & culture questions.",
        "Be prepared to classify Punjabi folk dances by gender: Bhangra, Jhumar, and Luddi (Male); Giddha, Sammi, and Jaago (Female)."
      ],
      "id": "hdzgwr8"
    },
